WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.125 --> 00:00:34.041


2
00:00:34.041 --> 00:00:38.166
<b>This is the final verse of the first chapter</b>
<b>of the Bhagavad Gita. </b>

3
00:00:38.166 --> 00:00:40.833
<b>Here, Sanjaya tells Dhritarashtra</b>

4
00:00:40.833 --> 00:00:45.166
<b>that Arjuna has finally abandoned</b>
<b>his bow and arrows,</b>

5
00:00:45.166 --> 00:00:48.500
<b>sitting down in the chariot,</b>
<b>overcome with despair.</b>

6
00:00:49.208 --> 00:00:53.333


7
00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:54.541
<b>Dilemma,</b>

8
00:00:54.541 --> 00:00:55.500
<b>anxiety,</b>

9
00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.500
<b>and ultimately despair</b>

10
00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:59.500
<b>and dejection.</b>

11
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:02.750
<b>Arjuna has gone through all these states.</b>

12
00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:06.375
<b>This first chapter of</b>
<b>the Bhagavad Gita is thus known as </b>

13
00:01:06.375 --> 00:01:10.208
<b>"Arjuna Vishada Yoga" </b>
<b>(The Yoga of Arjuna's Despair).</b>

14
00:01:10.208 --> 00:01:17.375
<b>The true value of light is understood not</b>
<b>in daylight, but when darkness falls.</b>

15
00:01:17.375 --> 00:01:18.541
<b>Similarly,</b>

16
00:01:18.541 --> 00:01:19.291
<b>the importance of dharma,</b>

17
00:01:19.291 --> 00:01:20.291
<b>wisdom,</b>

18
00:01:20.291 --> 00:01:20.958
<b>and knowledge</b>

19
00:01:20.958 --> 00:01:23.958
<b>is realized only when you're</b>

20
00:01:23.958 --> 00:01:26.916
<b>faced with a terrible obstacle.</b>

21
00:01:26.916 --> 00:01:30.416
<b>To counter this obstacle,</b>
<b>this despair of Arjuna,</b>

22
00:01:30.416 --> 00:01:34.125
<b>Krishna will now give teachings</b>
<b>in the following chapters,</b>

23
00:01:34.125 --> 00:01:40.791
<b>which will benefit not only Arjuna</b>
<b>but all of humanity.</b>

24
00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:45.625


25
00:01:45.625 --> 00:01:49.041
<b>Arjuna's Gandiva bow is his pride.</b>

26
00:01:49.041 --> 00:01:51.458
<b>It's not just a weapon,</b>

27
00:01:51.458 --> 00:01:56.458
<b>but a symbol of his talent</b>
<b>and limitless abilities.</b>

28
00:01:56.458 --> 00:01:57.708
<b>However,</b>

29
00:01:57.708 --> 00:02:02.458
<b>now that Arjuna is caught</b>
<b>in a whirlwind of emotions,</b>

30
00:02:02.458 --> 00:02:06.583
<b>even the Gandiva has slipped from his hand.</b>

31
00:02:06.583 --> 00:02:07.916
<b>His abilities,</b>

32
00:02:07.916 --> 00:02:10.791
<b>his talent</b>

33
00:02:10.791 --> 00:02:12.541
<b>seems useless.</b>

34
00:02:12.541 --> 00:02:17.708
<b>Arjuna's abandonment of his bow</b>
<b>and arrows symbolizes </b>

35
00:02:17.708 --> 00:02:21.458
<b>that true strength lies in the inner mind. </b>

36
00:02:21.458 --> 00:02:27.041
<b>It's this inner mind that directs the brain,</b>
<b>empowers the body,</b>

37
00:02:27.041 --> 00:02:32.875
<b>which then ultimately utilizes these abilities.</b>

38
00:02:32.875 --> 00:02:36.916
<b>If the guiding light itself goes out,</b>

39
00:02:36.916 --> 00:02:40.416
<b>anyone would lose their way.</b>

40
00:02:40.416 --> 00:02:44.000
<b>When we're drowning in negative thoughts,</b>

41
00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:46.458
<b>nothing goes right.</b>

42
00:02:46.458 --> 00:02:52.083
<b>While recognizing one's abilities</b>
<b>is a sign of competence,</b>

43
00:02:52.083 --> 00:02:55.791
<b>becoming humble in moments of doubt,</b>

44
00:02:55.791 --> 00:03:00.625
<b>bowing down and surrendering before a guru</b>

45
00:03:00.625 --> 00:03:06.958
<b>this too is a quality that Arjuna possesses in full.</b>

46
00:03:06.958 --> 00:03:13.416
<b>Arjuna has laid bare all the doubts</b>
<b>in his heart before me with an open mind.</b>

47
00:03:13.416 --> 00:03:17.208
<b>I will now address all of them.</b>

48
00:03:17.208 --> 00:03:21.583
<b>If you hide your ailment from a doctor,</b>

49
00:03:21.583 --> 00:03:25.375
<b>how can there be treatment?</b>

50
00:03:25.375 --> 00:03:26.416
<b>Therefore,</b>

51
00:03:26.416 --> 00:03:27.750
<b>don't hide,</b>

52
00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:29.833
<b>calm your ego,</b>

53
00:03:29.833 --> 00:03:31.958
<b>and in moments of severe doubt,</b>

54
00:03:31.958 --> 00:03:39.291
<b>do share your state of mind with</b>
<b>a well-wisher, a friend, or a guru.</b>

55
00:03:39.291 --> 00:03:41.791
<b>Solutions emerge from such humility.</b>

56
00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:47.208


57
00:03:47.208 --> 00:03:51.291
<b>If a pot is completely filled with dirty water,</b>

58
00:03:51.291 --> 00:03:56.125
<b>and clean water is poured into it from the top,</b>

59
00:03:56.125 --> 00:03:58.208
<b>what will happen?</b>

60
00:03:58.208 --> 00:04:03.125
<b>The clean water will spill over from the outside.</b>

61
00:04:03.125 --> 00:04:06.833
<b>The water in the pot will remain dirty, won't it?</b>

62
00:04:06.833 --> 00:04:09.125
<b>In this case, the right approach is</b>

63
00:04:09.125 --> 00:04:11.791
<b>to pour out all the dirty water,</b>

64
00:04:11.791 --> 00:04:13.583
<b>empty the pot completely,</b>

65
00:04:13.583 --> 00:04:15.291
<b>and then</b>

66
00:04:15.291 --> 00:04:18.750
<b>fill it with clean water.</b>

67
00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:20.875
<b>Similarly,</b>

68
00:04:20.875 --> 00:04:24.208
<b>when the mind is filled with negative thoughts,</b>

69
00:04:24.208 --> 00:04:30.291
<b>it's impossible for any inspiration</b>
<b>or knowledge to enter. </b>

70
00:04:30.291 --> 00:04:35.583
<b>A person immersed in pain needs people</b>

71
00:04:35.583 --> 00:04:40.458
<b>who encourage them to express</b>
<b>their state of mind,</b>

72
00:04:40.458 --> 00:04:42.916
<b>who listen to them with an open mind,</b>

73
00:04:42.916 --> 00:04:46.208
<b>without any criticism.</b>

74
00:04:46.208 --> 00:04:47.916
<b>Only when this happens</b>

75
00:04:47.916 --> 00:04:51.250
<b>can that person's mind be emptied,</b>

76
00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:56.750
<b>and only then can any guidance</b>
<b>or teaching be absorbed.</b>

77
00:04:56.750 --> 00:05:03.375
<b>I've listened to all of Arjuna's words so far,</b>

78
00:05:03.375 --> 00:05:06.708
<b>just with a smile.</b>

79
00:05:06.708 --> 00:05:08.750
<b>Now is the right time</b>

80
00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:10.916
<b>to explain to Arjuna,</b>

81
00:05:10.916 --> 00:05:12.500
<b>to awaken him,</b>

82
00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:15.125
<b>to show him the right path.</b>

83
00:05:15.125 --> 00:05:17.125
<b>You too,</b>

84
00:05:17.125 --> 00:05:20.458
<b>don't pour more water into an already full pot.</b>

85
00:05:20.458 --> 00:05:21.958
<b>Be patient,</b>

86
00:05:21.958 --> 00:05:24.125
<b>let that pot empty itself.</b>

87
00:05:24.125 --> 00:05:26.791
<b>And only after this happens,</b>

88
00:05:26.791 --> 00:05:28.541
<b>share your experiences,</b>

89
00:05:28.541 --> 00:05:30.583
<b>give your suggestions.</b>

90
00:05:30.583 --> 00:05:35.208
<b>Your goal is not to showcase your knowledge,</b>

91
00:05:35.208 --> 00:05:40.500
<b>your goal is for them to acquire your knowledge.</b>

92
00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:41.958
<b>Think about it.</b>

93
00:05:42.458 --> 00:05:49.291


94
00:05:49.291 --> 00:05:52.166
<b>or at your workplace,</b>

95
00:05:52.166 --> 00:05:56.333
<b>if someone who was previously</b>
<b>skilled in their work</b>

96
00:05:56.333 --> 00:06:01.166
<b>now makes occasional mistakes,</b>

97
00:06:01.166 --> 00:06:05.708
<b>or if their work quality has started to decline,</b>

98
00:06:05.708 --> 00:06:10.208
<b>the reason is likely not a lack of ability,</b>

99
00:06:10.208 --> 00:06:13.041
<b>but their state of mind.</b>

100
00:06:13.041 --> 00:06:16.291
<b>Some worry they're grappling with,</b>

101
00:06:16.291 --> 00:06:21.000
<b>some insecurity that has taken root in their mind,</b>

102
00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:23.000
<b>or some reason</b>

103
00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:27.208
<b>they've grown weary of this workplace.</b>

104
00:06:27.208 --> 00:06:33.666
<b>No skilled and capable person</b>
<b>becomes incompetent overnight.</b>

105
00:06:33.666 --> 00:06:37.875
<b>If you lead people in your organization,</b>

106
00:06:37.875 --> 00:06:43.083
<b>or if a colleague is going </b>
<b>through such a situation,</b>

107
00:06:43.083 --> 00:06:48.958
<b>it would be appropriate for you to try</b>
<b>to try to understand their feelings,</b>

108
00:06:48.958 --> 00:06:52.791
<b>to provide them mental</b>
<b>support during such times.</b>

109
00:06:52.791 --> 00:06:57.708
<b>Your behavior will give them the strength</b>
<b>to overcome their troubles,</b>

110
00:06:57.708 --> 00:07:01.833
<b>and will help ignite self-confidence within them.</b>

111
00:07:01.833 --> 00:07:05.875
<b>This is not only necessary for</b>
<b>the organization's objectives,</b>

112
00:07:05.875 --> 00:07:07.125
<b>but </b>

113
00:07:07.125 --> 00:07:11.458
<b>it's also right from a humanitarian perspective.</b>

114
00:07:11.458 --> 00:07:15.583
<b>It will also strengthen mutual trust and harmony.</b>

